  "description": "OK, list of 'Dos and Don'ts' during the great Covid rap battle: Don't go to gyms, don't take public transport, don't use ride shares, don't go to concerts, don't go to sporting events, crowded public places... don't this... don't that...DO ride a bike. Get out, enjoy, zip around the neighborhood, zing your way to your socially distant work office, the grocery store during off hours... errands... More DO, less DON'T. Do the DO with the LXI T i/O -- everything needed for easy, quick transportation: built-in rack, even comes with a bungee -- even has button-activated lights, a throttle for getting up to speed, engine cut-off brakes, an easygoing 350W hub motor, fenders, kickstand.. the list goes on and it's all-inclusive. Turnkey simplicity, look no further. Everything you need, nothing you don't, at an astounding value.\nThrottle allows for versatility and ease of starting when loaded down with groceries/supplies\nRobust 8-speed drivetrain resists torque-based e-bike wear through a thicker chain\n14.5Ah/522Wh battery provides plenty capacity for greater distances, loaded travel, and throttle usage\nE-bike specific Tektro HD-E350 hydraulic brakes have an engine cut-off built in for worry free e-bike riding\nBuilt-in rear rack melds utilitarian simplicity with aesthetics\nClass 2 e-bike: throttle only or pedal assist up to 20mph",
